    "paragraph": "Neighborhood Deprivation Shapes Post-Flood Population Losses in Pune and Bandung analyzes mobile phone device presence across 30-day windows surrounding floods to reveal that post-flood mobility tracks neighborhood deprivation levels. Multi-Scale Spatio-Temporal Exploratory Analysis of Urban Vehicle Theft examines 521,098 stolen-vehicle reports in Los Angeles from 2000 to 2022, finding that 10.8% of 250 m cells account for half of all incidents and six census tracts persist as hotspots for 23 consecutive years. Beyond urban boundaries: Percolation reveals land-consumptive growth in India applies an unrestricted DBSCAN percolation framework to 100-m grid cells from 1975 to 2025 to define city boundaries across India's 50 largest urban agglomerations.",
